        "id": 1003247
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-09T19:22:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Another possibility would be to do:\n\n        {\n\t\t.procname\t\u003d \"bpf_disable_prog_load\",\n\t\t.data\t\t\u003d \u0026sysctl_bpf_disable_prog_load,\n\t\t.maxlen\t\t\u003d sizeof(sysctl_bpf_disable_prog_load),\n\t\t.mode\t\t\u003d 0644,\n\t\t.proc_handler\t\u003d proc_dointvec_minmax,\n\t\t.extra1\t\t\u003d \u0026sysctl_bpf_disable_prog_load_lock,\n\t\t.extra2\t\t\u003d SYSCTL_ONE,\n\t},\n        {\n\t\t.procname\t\u003d \"bpf_disable_prog_load_lock\",\n\t\t.data\t\t\u003d \u0026sysctl_bpf_disable_prog_load_lock,\n\t\t.maxlen\t\t\u003d sizeof(sysctl_bpf_disable_prog_load_lock),\n\t\t.mode\t\t\u003d 0644,\n\t\t.proc_handler\t\u003d proc_dointvec_minmax,\n\t\t.extra1\t\t\u003d SYSCTL_ONE,\n\t\t.extra2\t\t\u003d SYSCTL_ONE,\n\t},\n\n(both start at boot time 0)\n\nNow the first one is the enable/disable, while the second one is the lock/fuse.\n\nWe always flip the first one once platform bpf loading is done, but we only flip the fuse on \u0027user\u0027 builds.",
      "parentUuid": "90314b3a_f6c5947b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 6529,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 6530,
        "endChar": 24
